rn Java that flourished in the eleventh and twelfth centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kedu-plain"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kedu-plain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kedu Plain</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kedu Plain is a fertile volcanic basin in Central Java, Indonesia, ringed by the volcanoes Merapi, Merbabu, Sumbing and Sindoro.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kedukan-bukit-inscription"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kedukan-bukit-inscription.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kedukan Bukit inscription</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Kedukan Bukit inscription is a stone inscription dated 682 CE, found near Palembang in Sumatra.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/keelung"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/keelung.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Keelung</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Keelung is a port city on the northern tip of Taiwan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kefalonia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kefalonia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kefalonia</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Kefalonia (Cephalonia) is the largest of the Ionian Islands, off the west coast of Greece.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/kefe-eyalet"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kefe-eyalet.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Kefe Eyalet</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">Kefe Eyalet was the Ottoman province on the